  "correction_id": "A-COR-0003",
  "rule_id": "A-R-012",
  "note": "Don't carry them forward. First check whether the missing count sheets were combined onto another deposit slip. If these are clearly route cash, send all four to the ops manager to find the sheets, since each one is well over the $20 threshold. If you can't tell they're route cash, treat them as unidentified deposits of $50 or more and send them to me (Marv), not to 4990.",
  "explanation": "The controller said unmatched branch deposits are not carried forward. The investigator first checks whether the count sheets were combined onto another deposit slip. Deposits that are clearly route cash and over the $20 threshold go to the ops manager. Deposits of $50 or more that can't be identified as route cash are treated as unidentified and go to the owner (Marv), not to 4990. A-R-012 is narrowed to the route-cash case and approved. A new rule placed right after it covers the unidentified case. Neither can be executable, because the rule language can't judge whether a deposit is route cash or find a combined slip."
 }
